{
  "description": "Shared host memory_candidate_result bridge mappings. Pending emits one terminal successful effect resolution with only the candidate arm; accepted emits only the record receipt arm. These tests do not exercise kernel idempotency or receipt validation inside the kernel.",
  "mapping_notes": [
    "Pending requires nonempty string candidate_id and receipt_id; accepted requires nonempty string record_ref and digest but does not require candidate IDs.",
    "Missing or invalid receipt fields fail non-retryably with storage_unavailable.",
    "Every provided non-null error takes precedence and fails retryably. String messages are unchanged; other JSON values use compact JSON with recursively sorted object keys and unescaped Unicode.",
    "Rejected and fallback statuses fail non-retryably; reason_code must be a nonempty string, otherwise unspecified."
  ],
  "binding_id": "fixture-memory",
  "effect_id": "effect-7",
  "cases": [
    {
